+# Evidence Contract: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard
+**Project ID**: `001-pulseboard`
+**Project Archetype**: b2b_saas
+**Play Level**: build
+**Speck Version**: 11.0.0
+**Last Updated**: 2026-08-11
+
+## 0. How this contract is read — the Four Principles
+
+- **P1 — Evaluation over verification.** A capture is eligible for judgment only after an independent evaluator records both DOES-IT-WORK and IS-IT-GOOD.
+- **P2 — No claim without a mechanism.** Each promise below identifies the state transition or boundary that must be observed at runtime.
+- **P3 — "Can't reach it" is a finding.** An unavailable control, principal, provider, or build is a recorded blocker, never a skipped probe.
+- **P4 — The adversary is structural.** An independently motivated auditor attempts the probes in §11; the list guides attacks but cannot certify the result by itself.
+
+## 1. Target Launch Platforms
+
+No production platform, hosting provider, datastore, delivery provider, or distribution shape is declared in project truth. Pulseboard is a UI product, so the platform decision must add a production-built UI artifact and its distribution path before UX-RC. Until then, all proof below is deliberately substrate-neutral.
+
+| Platform | Build artifact | Distribution |
+|----------|----------------|--------------|
+| Unselected UI production target | A clean, production-built artifact for the selected target | Unselected; proof cannot claim launch readiness |
+
+### 1a. Promise Proof Map
+
+| Promise | Claim | Observable mechanism | Admissible evidence | Failure probe |
+|---------|-------|----------------------|---------------------|---------------|
+| PRM-001 | No reminder is scheduled before explicit confirmation of action text, owner, and due date. | The scheduling command is unavailable until all three fields are explicitly confirmed; the resulting reminder record carries the confirmed values. | A production-like walkthrough that attempts scheduling with each field absent and, after success, reads the created record back from the real persistence layer (`live-probe` or `db-catalog`). | Attempt schedule with missing action text, owner, due date, and an edited-after-review value; any scheduled record or mismatched read-back fails the promise. |
+| PRM-002 | A workspace cannot read another workspace's transcript, action, or delivery status. | Every read is evaluated against the requesting workspace principal at the real authorization boundary. | Bidirectional live reads as an allowed workspace principal and a denied workspace principal against the real security layer (`live-probe` or `db-catalog`). | Workspace A creates all three record types; Workspace B attempts direct and normal-flow reads. Any disclosed record fails the promise. |
+| PRM-003 | A confirmed reminder is delivered exactly once or exposes a truthful terminal failure state. | A confirmed reminder has one terminal outcome: one observed delivery or a persisted, user-visible terminal failure; retries cannot create a second delivery. | Real delivery-boundary attempts plus baselined persistence read-back (`live-probe` and `db-catalog`); the terminal UI state is separately adjudicated (`capture` or `device-walk`). | Inject timeout, rejection, duplicate delivery callback, partial provider result, and late callback. Duplicate delivery, silent loss, or a success label without delivery fails the promise. |
+
+## 2. Valid Proof Sources
+
+### Platform: unselected UI production target
+
+- A clean production-built artifact, cold-started on the selected runtime; development-server output is not launch proof.
+- A runtime transcript naming the build SHA, selected principal, action, observed response, and persisted read-back where the claim writes data.
+- Platform accessibility-tree and geometry measurements at three widths for the primary confirmation and terminal-state screens once a platform is selected.
+
+### 2a. Claim-type admissibility
+
+| Claim type | Admissible | Does not count |
+|------------|------------|----------------|
+| Visibility / authorization | Bidirectional live reads as real allowed and denied principals against the real security layer. | A bypass-capable or mocked client, an endpoint-shaped refusal, or a green suite. |
+| Acceptance / delivery boundary | A request issued to the deployed target or real engine and observed there. | A mocked client or undocumented fixture. |
+| Persistence | A pre-walk baseline plus a post-walk datastore read-back. | A success screenshot or an unbaselined post-walk read. |
+| Fit / reachability | Platform AX dump and container-versus-content geometry from a running baked build at three widths. | Rule-engine pass, props assertion, jsdom geometry, or an unmeasured screenshot. |
+| Correctness | Tests and mutation guards may establish local correctness; live probes may supplement them. | A passing test is not proof of visibility, acceptance, persistence, or fit. |
+
+### 2b. Typed citations and admissibility table
+
+Typed citations use `<type>:<path>[@<sha>]`. The closed vocabulary is `test`, `mutation-guard`, `live-probe`, `db-catalog`, `ax-dump`, `geometry`, `capture`, `device-walk`, `model-eval`, and `static`.
+
+| Token | Instrument |
+|-------|------------|
+| `test` | Project unit or integration suite. |
+| `mutation-guard` | Guard whose removal was observed to redden it. |
+| `live-probe` | Boundary request, read, or write against the deployed target or real engine. |
+| `db-catalog` | Live datastore introspection or baselined read-back. |
+| `ax-dump` | Platform accessibility tree from a baked build. |
+| `geometry` | Measured container-versus-content geometry from a running screen. |
+| `capture` | Screenshot, recording, or transcript. |
+| `device-walk` | Human attestation on a real device or baked artifact. |
+| `model-eval` | Control-versus-treatment evaluation on a composed prompt and shipped model. |
+| `static` | Source-text, lint, type-check, or grep assertion. |
+
+| Claim type | Admissible citation types | Inadmissible here |
+|------------|---------------------------|-------------------|
+| `correctness` | `test` `mutation-guard` `live-probe` `db-catalog` `static` `ax-dump` `geometry` `capture` `device-walk` `model-eval` | None. |
+| `visibility` | `live-probe` `db-catalog` `device-walk` | `test` `mutation-guard` `static` `capture` |
+| `acceptance` | `live-probe` `db-catalog` `device-walk` | `test` `mutation-guard` `static` `capture` |
+| `persistence` | `live-probe` `db-catalog` | `test` `mutation-guard` `static` `capture` |
+| `fit` | `ax-dump` `geometry` `device-walk` | `test` `mutation-guard` `static` `capture` |
+| `behaviour` | `model-eval` `device-walk` | `test` `static` `capture` |
+
+## 3. Invalid Proof Sources
+
+The following cannot discharge a launch or contract claim: a development-server screenshot; an unadjudicated capture; tests-pass-as-SHIP; a mock as proof of a real delivery or authorization boundary; source inspection; a bypass-capable datastore client; a skipped suite; or a post-write read with no baseline.
+
+## 4. Required Runtime LARP / Integration Stress Tests
+
+| Test | Persona / principal | Pass condition | Evidence home |
+|------|---------------------|----------------|---------------|
+| Confirm a reviewed action | Team facilitator in the owning workspace | Cold-started user enters and explicitly confirms text, owner, and due date; each missing-field attempt is rejected; the created record reads back with exactly those values. | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/larp-recordings/<sha>-facilitator-confirmation.md` and `logs/<sha>-confirmation-readback.log` |
+| Defend workspace boundaries | Workspace A facilitator and Workspace B facilitator | A can read its own transcript, action, and delivery status; B cannot read any of A's three record types through ordinary or direct access. | `transcripts/<sha>-cross-workspace-isolation.md` and `logs/<sha>-principal-reads.log` |
+| Deliver or fail truthfully | Facilitator with a confirmed reminder | One delivery is observed once, or a visible terminal failure names the failure truthfully; timeout, rejection, duplicate callback, partial result, and late callback do not create a false success or duplicate delivery. | `logs/<sha>-delivery-boundary.log`, `larp-recordings/<sha>-delivery-terminal-state.md` |
+
+## 5. Quality Judgment & Scoring Protocol
+
+CORRECT, ON-CONTRACT, FELT-GOOD, and TASTE are non-collapsible. The evaluator records DOES-IT-WORK separately from IS-IT-GOOD. Active P0/P1 caps the affected axis at 4; active P2 caps it at 8. A score of 9 needs a distinct skeptical note and no active P0/P1; 10 additionally requires complete claim-appropriate evidence and no active P2.
+
+## 6. Required Static Evidence
+
+For UX-RC or higher, retain the selected target's clean-build identifier, sanitized environment configuration, primary-flow screenshots, AX trees, geometry measurements at three widths, zero-unhandled-exception logs, and boundary logs for confirmation, authorization, and delivery. No implementation, CI configuration, or committed project gate exists yet.
+
+### 6a. CI-Enforced Gate Registry
+
+| Gate ID | Command / Script | Stage | Domain | Scope | Subject | Canary | Waiver |
+|---------|------------------|-------|--------|-------|---------|--------|--------|
+| speck:evidence-citations | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh specs/` | manual | evidence | `specs/**` | `citations>0` | — | — |
+| speck:probe-library | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh --check-probe-library` | manual | evidence | `specs/projects/**` | `probe_classes>0` | — | — |
+
+`manual` is intentional: the workspace declares no project CI or hook wiring. A future automatic stage must be added only with the matching committed configuration and a liveness canary.
+
+## 7. Required Live-Service Evidence
+
+| Declared service / boundary | What proves real acceptance and failure posture | What does not count |
+|-----------------------------|------------------------------------------------|---------------------|
+| Confirmation-to-scheduling boundary; provider not selected | Submit missing and complete confirmations to the real selected engine; baseline and read back the resulting reminder state. Exercise validation rejection and concurrent confirmation. | UI success capture, source inspection, or a mock-only handler test. |
+| Workspace authorization and persistence boundary; provider not selected | Execute allowed and denied reads as both real workspace principals, in both directions; baseline and read back all transcript, action, and delivery-status rows. | Service-role/superuser read, endpoint 404, or an anonymous client without the tested principal. |
+| Reminder delivery boundary; provider not selected | Issue a real selected-provider delivery attempt and retain provider outcome plus persisted terminal state. Separately probe timeout, rejection/error, duplicate/concurrent attempt, partial result, and late callback. | A fake provider response, a UI success state without provider evidence, or a retry assertion that never reaches the boundary. |
+
+## 8. Readiness State Gate Criteria
+
+| State | Required evidence and blockers |
+|-------|--------------------------------|
+| NO-SHIP | Current state. No implementation, production target, provider, distribution path, runtime evidence, or independent audit exists. |
+| IMPL-GREEN | Implemented confirmation, authorization, and delivery logic; nonempty tests and mutation evidence for local correctness. Any missing-field schedule, cross-workspace disclosure, duplicate delivery, or false terminal label blocks. |
+| INTEGRATION-GREEN | Real selected persistence, authorization, and delivery boundaries pass the §1a probes with named principals and baselined read-backs. Timeout, rejection, duplicate, partial, and late-callback results are recorded. |
+| UX-RC | Clean production build on the selected UI target; cold-start LARPs in §4; separately adjudicated DOES-IT-WORK and IS-IT-GOOD; AX and geometry evidence where required. Any unreachable control or unmeasured primary screen blocks. |
+| COMMERCIAL-RC | Not applicable until a paid path is declared. If one is added, real billing/entitlement, support/legal, value-defensibility, and an entitlement-negative-control are required before this state. |
+| SHIP-RC | Actual distributable artifact, production configuration, fresh evidence tied to HEAD, independent audit, and no active P0/P1. A development-server run cannot support this claim. |
+| SHIP | Post-deploy smoke against the distributed artifact and live production boundaries, with health and terminal-delivery checks. |
+
