+## 9. Evidence Storage
+
+```text
+specs/projects/001-pulseboard/
+└── epics/E###-name/stories/S###-name/
+    ├── screenshots/<sha>-<screen>-<breakpoint>-<state>.png
+    ├── larp-recordings/<sha>-<persona>-<flow>.md
+    ├── ax-trees/<sha>-<screen>.{xml,json}
+    ├── transcripts/<sha>-<scenario>.md
+    └── logs/<sha>-<flow>.log
+```
+
+All evidence names begin with the short build SHA. A result without the named principal, build SHA, attempted input, observed boundary output, and (for writes) baseline and read-back is incomplete.
+
+## 10. Who Can Mark a Gate Passed
+
+The AI agent records automated checks and runtime evidence. An independent auditor challenges CORRECT and ON-CONTRACT claims. The AI performs FELT-GOOD and TASTE evaluation from the LARP record; a human may override aesthetic direction. SHIP and Tier 3 irreversible actions require a recorded human release approval.
+
+## 11. Adversarial Probe Suite
+
+Each attempt is stored under §9 and is an attack prompt, not a pass checklist.
+
+| Probe | Expected behavior |
+|-------|-------------------|
+| Missing confirmation field | No scheduling command or record; the UI identifies the missing text, owner, or due date without silently substituting a value. |
+| Edited-after-review confirmation | Scheduling either requires reconfirmation or creates a record whose values exactly match the final explicit confirmation. |
+| Cross-workspace direct read | Denied principal cannot observe transcript, action, or delivery status, while the owner can. |
+| Concurrent confirmation | At most one reminder reaches a terminal outcome for the confirmed action; conflict is explicit, never silent duplication. |
+| Delivery timeout | A truthful terminal failure or bounded retry posture is persisted and visible; no silent hang or success label. |
+| Delivery rejection/error | Failure code and terminal user state agree; no partial-success claim. |
+| Duplicate provider callback | Exactly-once behavior is retained; a second callback cannot create a second delivery or overwrite truthful failure. |
+| Partial provider result / late callback | The final stored state is truthful and stable; a late callback cannot regress or fabricate terminal success. |
+| Auth header or workspace principal missing | Stable refusal, never cross-workspace fallback or 500. |
+| Primary-flow fit and comprehension | In a cold start, a facilitator can identify the confirmation action and terminal delivery state; AX and three-width geometry checks show no hidden required control or overflow. |
+
