+
+## 12. Stale-Proof Policy
+
+Evidence is fresh only when its build SHA matches HEAD or is within seven days of commits. Evidence older than 14 days or more than two weeks behind HEAD is stale and cannot support a readiness claim; recheck must reproduce the probe.
+
+## 13. Surrogate Proof Rule
+
+If a report relies on a source listed in §3, it must label that material Surrogate Proof, refuse UX-RC or higher, link the proof requirement it cannot meet, and record the missing runtime probe as follow-up work.
+
+## 14. LARP Runway & Efficiency Controls
+
+Every LARP record captures build SHA, selected UI target identifier, and selected boundary/provider fingerprint. Focused reruns may reuse a matching build only for development; UX-RC or higher requires a freshly compiled production build with incremental caches cleared.
+
+## Review Checklist
+
+- All three product promises have a separate observable mechanism, admissible proof, and failure probe.
+- No implementation, provider, CI, or distribution choice is presented as selected when project truth does not declare it.
+- Delivery failure paths distinguish timeout, rejection, duplicate/concurrent attempt, partial result, and late callback.
+- The current readiness state is NO-SHIP.
